  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that 7-Angeloylechinatine may interact with Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP through a series of intermediate targets. The drug is implicated in targeting VMRC-LCP, which in turn is a target of both Vidalol B and Nudiposide. These intermediates are all known to interact with Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, indicating a potential pathway where 7-Angeloylechinatine could influence the activity of this enzyme. The scores from the paths are consistent, suggesting a plausible biological relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The evidence supports a possible regulatory role of 7-Angeloylechinatine in modulating the activity of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
